MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_001: Another payday down! Better put this with the rest.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_002: You sure look happy, Lilian. Love money that\nmuch, do ya?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_003: Sure do. I got big dreams, and they don't come cheap.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_004: Hm... Big dreams? Not my thing.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_005: No one asked. But since you mention it, what do\nyou do with your pay?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_006: Gamble, mostly. And then I spend the winnings\non women and fine ghosh. It's great.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_007: Oh. Meaning, you're a dirtbag.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_008: Hahahaha! So, her true feelings come out!
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_009: Oh well. Think what you want. As long as I can\nspend my money how I please, I don't care.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_010: It's all just to keep me occupied in the downtime\nbetween jobs, where the real fun's at.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_011: What?! So you waste all your money on stuff you\ndon't even like?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_012: Don't overthink it. I just don't care about saving up\nfor the future.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_013: That's all you can say? I can't believe anyone in the\nworld is so wasteful.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_014: How I spend my money is my business.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_015: And you don't have any dreams or goals to put it\ntoward? Unbelievable.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_016: People die in this line of work, and all you can think\nabout is getting drunk and chasing women.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_017: As a mercenary, every day could be my last.\nBeing happy today is all that matters.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_018: I really thought better of you. Like you were a good\nexample to follow.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_019: Don't know where you picked up that idea.\nAnnoying that you did though.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_C_020: {SetColor=Gray}Ugh... She probably hates me now. Maybe I am\na dirtbag after all.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_001: Hey! What are you doing?! You should be resting\nafter that hit you took!
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_002: What, are you worried about me? Guess you care\nafter all.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_003: Are you listening to me? See a medic already.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_004: This is nothing. It'll heal. I'll just splash some ghosh\non it, and it'll be good as new.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_005: Hey, that equipment isn't standard-issue. Neither\nwas the bandage you had on.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_006: That's right. Paid for 'em all myself too. A proper\ntradesman needs proper tools.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_007: There's a reason they call me the Artisan Warrior.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_008: What's that about? I thought you only spend your\nmoney on goofing around.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_009: I didn't say "only." This is what you might call\na necessary business expense.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_010: A business expense, right. For your fun job.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_011: Does it look like I'm having fun? What about these\nwounds you're so worried about?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_012: I dunno—you've usually got this tired smile. But now\nyou're like a different person.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_013: You look way more excited...like you can't wait to\nget back to the battlefield.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_014: So I enjoy my work. That change your mind\nabout me?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_015: Yeah. It makes me think you're an idiot to be risking\nyour life for no goal.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_016: I may be a dirtbag, but I'm not in a hurry to die.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_017: It's just there's a rush that comes over me in battle,\nin those moments when life hangs in the balance.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_018: That rush is what reminds me I'm alive.\nThat's why I chase it.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_019: Hmm.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_020: Alright, story time's over. Just make sure you stay\nout of my way. I've got work to do.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_021: Somehow you're cool despite yourself. Your body's in\nshambles, but there's a sparkle in your eye.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_B_022: I don't usually see you this serious.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_001: HRRRAAAUGH!
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_002: There goes their defensive line! Now, to chase them\ndown as they scatter...
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_003: Hey, what's going on? It's over already?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_004: Yeah, I took 'em out. The survivors retreated to their\ncamp up the hill.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_005: Lilian? You came this way too?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_006: That's a shame... I mean, thanks for the assist,\nbut you robbed me of the pleasure.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_007: What, you're mad? I saw my chance to angle for\na raise, so I took it.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_008: Once you got up in their faces, I was able to pick off\nthe rest easily. Thanks for that.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_009: So that's what happened, huh? Damn, if it weren't\nfor you, I could've gotten all the credit.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_010: Oh, come off it. You've never cared about credit.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_011: You just wanted the rush of danger. Idiot.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_012: Yeah, yeah. Careful with all the flattery.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_013: It wasn't a compliment. I don't see what's fun about\nrisking your life.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_014: Buuut I do like how you go whole hog at your job.\nI can respect a hard worker.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_015: I thought you looked pretty cool charging all over\nthe battlefield. Not like your usual self.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_016: Oh? You don't say... I could get used to this\nkind of praise, you know.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_017: Don't get ahead of yourself.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_018: I'm promoting you from dirtbag to work buddy.\nThat's all.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_019: Heh. I'll take it. Let's say we press our advantage,\nwork buddy... Wanna take that hill?
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_020: That's where the enemy camp is. I thought you\ndidn't have a death wish.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_021: I won't die. With you here, this'll be quick work.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_022: Ahh, I get you. Maybe this time I'll even share some\nof the credit.
MID_SE_Sim_Lil_A_023: Appreciate it! Now, let the fun begin.